course: dictionary
lesson: 12259
title: Contaminated and contaminate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Contaminated means made dirty, impure or harmful because something has got mixed in, such as germs, poison or chemicals. «The water in the flood was contaminated, so nobody was allowed to drink it.» The clues are the flood and the warning not to drink it, so the water is not safe.
explain: Contaminate is the verb. To contaminate something is to make it dirty or harmful. «Raw chicken can contaminate the salad if it touches it.» Try your meaning in the sentence: "Raw chicken can make the salad dirty or harmful." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Always ask: what would fit here? Words like germs, poison, chemicals and "not safe to drink" are clues that something has gone wrong. When you read contaminated, look for the thing that was mixed in.
fact: Contaminated means made dirty, impure or harmful by something mixed in.
fact: «Contaminated» is an adjective, and «contaminate» is the verb, as in «Germs can contaminate food».
fact: «Contaminated water» can make people ill, so it must be cleaned or thrown away.
fact: Scientists keep their experiments clean so that they are not contaminated by something unwanted.
fact: Wash your hands and chopping boards after raw meat, so it does not contaminate other food.
exercise: «The water in the old well was contaminated, so the village could not drink it.» What does contaminated mean here? | Frozen solid | Full of fish | Clear and cold from the spring | *Made dirty or harmful by something mixed in
exercise: «Raw meat can contaminate other food if you do not wash the board.» What does contaminate mean? | To put something into a box | *To make something dirty or harmful | To make something look nicer | To cook something slowly
exercise: «Doctors tested the river water, which was contaminated with germs.» What was the water contaminated with? | Sand | Pebbles | Sunshine | *Germs
test: Ruby said, «Don't eat that sandwich, it's contaminated.» What does Ruby mean? | *It has been made harmful by something mixed in | It is freshly made | It is cold | It is very tasty
test: «The lab kept the samples clean so they would not become contaminated.» What is the main idea? | *Keeping samples clean stops them being harmed by something mixed in | Samples should be left out in the sun | Samples must always be mixed together | Samples are always safe to eat
exam: Which sentence uses contaminated correctly? | *The milk was contaminated with germs, so we poured it away. | My shoes were contaminated because they were brand new. | The sunny afternoon was contaminated with laughter. | The song was contaminated by a lovely, clear tune.
